          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Bott periodicity
            is the name of a periodicity phenomenon that appears throughout
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+geometry"} spin geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
          %h3#in_topological_ktheory In topological K-theory
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+K-theory"} reduced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            groups have a degree-2 periodicity:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msubsup
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tilde K_{\mathbb{C}}^\bullet(X)
                  \\simeq
                  \\tilde K_{\mathbb{C}}^{\bullet + 2}(X)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This isomorphism is induced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/external+tensor+product"} external tensor product
            with the image of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basic+line+bundle+on+the+2-sphere"} basic line bundle on the 2-sphere
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+K-theory"} reduced K-theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bott+element"} Bott element
          %p
            For details see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "topological+K-theory#BottPeriodicity"} Bott periodicity
          %p
            The periodicity lifts to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+spaces"} classifying spaces
            and makes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} representing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            of complex K-theory be an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+periodic+ring+spectrum"} even periodic ring spectrum
          %p
            In particular the 2-periodicity in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+unitary+group"} stable unitary group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_n U(n)
            is thus a shadow of Bott periodicity.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi i
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mtext even
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi i
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mtext odd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_i(U) = \pi_i(GL_{\mathbb{C}})
                  \=
                  \\left\lbrace
                  \\array{
                  0 &amp;\vert&amp; i\, \text{even}
                  \\\
                  \\mathbb{Z} &amp;\vert&amp; i \, \text{odd}
                  }
                  \\right.
          %p
            Similarly the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+K-theory"} reduced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            groups have an 8-periodicity
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msubsup
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tilde K^\bullet_{\mathbb{R}}(X)
                  \\simeq
                  \\tilde K^{\bullet + 8}_{\mathbb{R}}( X )
          %p
            a shadow of which is the 8-periodicity in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+orthogonal+group"} stable orthogonal group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mtext mod
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mn 8
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ℤ
                              %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 1
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mtext mod
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mn 8
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 2
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mtext mod
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mn 8
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 3
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mtext mod
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mn 8
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 4
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mtext mod
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mn 8
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 5
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mtext mod
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mn 8
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 6
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mtext mod
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mn 8
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 7
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mtext mod
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_i( O )
                  \=
                  \\pi_i(GL_{\mathbb{R}})
                  \=
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbb{Z}_2 &amp;\vert&amp; i = 0 \, \text{mod}\, 8
                  \\\
                  \\mathbb{Z}_2 &amp;\vert&amp; i = 1 \, \text{mod}\, 8
                  \\\
                  0 &amp;\vert&amp; i = 2 \, \text{mod}\, 8
                  \\\
                  \\mathbb{Z} &amp;\vert&amp; i = 3 \, \text{mod}\, 8
                  \\\
                  0 &amp;\vert&amp; i = 4 \, \text{mod}\, 8
                  \\\
                  0 &amp;\vert&amp; i = 5 \, \text{mod}\, 8
                  \\\
                  0 &amp;\vert&amp; i = 6 \, \text{mod}\, 8
                  \\\
                  \\mathbb{Z} &amp;\vert&amp; i = 7 \, \text{mod}\, 8
                  }
                  \\right.
          %h3#in_spin_geometry In Spin geometry
          %p
            The complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+algebras"} Clifford algebras
            repeat – up to
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+equivalence"} Morita equivalence
            – with period 2,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cl
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Morita
                    %msub
                      %mi Cl
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl_{n}(\mathbb{C}) \simeq_{Morita} Cl_{n+2}(\mathbb{C})
          %p
            The real Clifford algebras analogously have period 8,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cl
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Morita
                    %msub
                      %mi Cl
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 8
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl_n(\mathbb{R}) \simeq_{Morita} Cl_{n+8}(\mathbb{R})
          %p
            Accordingly the basic properties of complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+representations"} spinor representations
            are the same for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(d-1,1)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo +
                    %mn 2
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(d+2-1,1)
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ten-fold+way"} ten-fold way
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+fibration"} Hopf fibration
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/periodic+cohomology+theory"} periodic cohomology theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry+and+division+algebras"}> supersymmetry and division algebras
                \.
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The original statement as periodicity of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+Lie+groups"} classical Lie groups
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raoul+Bott"}> Raoul Bott
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Stable Homotopy of the Classical Groups
                %strong 43
                10 (1957) 933-935 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/89403"}> jstor:89403
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eldon+Dyer"}> Eldon Dyer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Lashof"} Richard Lashof
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A topological Proof of the Bott Periodicity Theorems
                %strong 54
                (1961) 231–254 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02415354"}> doi:10.1007/BF02415354
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Proof of Bott periodicity for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Bott periodicity and the index of elliptic operators
              %strong 19
              1 (1968) 113–140 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/qmath/19.1.113"}> doi:10.1093/qmath/19.1.113
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li#Segal68
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
                , Prop. 3.2 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Equivariant K-theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/PMIHES_1968__34__129_0"} numdam:PMIHES_1968__34__129_0
            %li#Karoubi05
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Karoubi"}> Max Karoubi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Bott Periodicity in Topological, Algebraic and Hermitian K-Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Friedlander"} Eric Friedlander
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Grayson"} Daniel Grayson
                (eds.)
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+K-Theory"} Handbook of K-Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-27855-9_4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-540-27855-9_4
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dai+Tamaki"}> Dai Tamaki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akira+Kono"} Akira Kono
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generalized Cohomology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/mmono-230"} ISBN: 978-0-8218-3514-2
            %li#HJJS08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dale+Husem%C3%B6ller"}> Dale Husemöller
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Joachim"} Michael Joachim
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Branislav+Jur%C4%8Do"} Branislav Jurčo
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schottenloher"} Martin Schottenloher
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Basic+Bundle+Theory+and+K-Cohomology+Invariants"} Basic Bundle Theory and K-Cohomology Invariants
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 726
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~schotten/Texte/978-3-540-74955-4_Book_LNP726.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-540-74956-1"} doi:10.1007/978-3-540-74956-1
          %p For a list of proofs of Bott periodicity, see
          %ul
            %li
              %em> Proofs of Bott periodicity
              ,
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/q/8800/447"} MO
